# Adaptations and other relationships: Murder on the Orient Express
#
# Agatha Christie's novel (1934) and the works and expressions derived from it,
# chosen to show the different relationships RDA has between works and between
# expressions. Each statement is made in one direction only; the inverse
# ("har bearbeidelse til spillefilm", "har oversettelse" ...) is inferred.
#
# Same work, new expression:
#   - the English original, two Norwegian translations (Axel S. Seeberg 1975,
#     Ola Halvor Seeberg Nygård 2012), each "er oversettelse av" the original
#   - an abridged English reader (Collins ELT, level B1), "er forkortelse av"
#     the original. RDA also allows an abridgement to be treated as a work of
#     its own (rdawo:P10125): a point for discussion.
#   - audiobooks: English read by Dan Stevens (2013) and Kenneth Branagh (2017),
#     Norwegian read by John Yngvar Fearnley (1992, Seeberg's translation) and
#     Bjørn Fougner (2017, Nygård's translation). A reading is an expression of
#     its own (spoken word); RDA has no relationship "is a reading of", so the
#     text read is named only in the note.
#
# New works, related to the novel (work level):
#   - motion pictures, Sidney Lumet 1974 and Kenneth Branagh 2017
#     (er bearbeidelse til spillefilm). The 2017 film is often called a remake,
#     but both adapt the novel; whether to add "er nyinnspilling av" is left
#     open.
#   - television, Agatha Christie's Poirot 2010 (er bearbeidelse for fjernsyn),
#     an episode that is part of a series work
#   - radio, BBC Radio 4 1992 (er bearbeidelse for radio)
#   - stage play, Ken Ludwig 2017 (er dramatisering av)
#   - graphic novel, Eckartsberg and Chaiko 2017 (er bearbeidelse til
#     tegneserieroman), French, with a Norwegian translation (expression level)
#   - computer game, 2006 (er bearbeidelse av, the general relationship, since
#     RDA has none for games)
#   - Disney parody, Topolino sull'Orient Express 1985 (er parodi av). The story
#     is a jewel theft, not a murder: parody, imitation or only inspiration?
#   - study guide, Gale 2016 (er veiledning til)
#   - the notes and glossary in the Collins reader (er supplement til), a work
#     of their own embodied in the same book as the abridged text
#
# Not recorded, as exercises: the French and other translations, the 2001 CBS
# film, the 2023 computer game, the manifestations of the plays and the TV
# episode, the 1934 first editions' extent, Richard Rodney Bennett's film
# music.
#
# Sources: Nasjonalbiblioteket (api.nb.no) for the Norwegian editions, library
# catalogues and the publishers for the others. Identifiers are ad hoc
# (http://example.org/orient/...).

